      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@35429",
      "type": "passage",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "What are those?",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@35429/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 15,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 6661687,
        "end": 6661727,
        "line": 249956,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap38/p@35429",
        "anchor": "sceneI_38.4"
      },
      "speakerLabel": null,
      "attribution": {
        "status": "source-unlabelled"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@35473",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "HERALD.\nMen of great quality, as may be judged\nBy their appointment. Some of Thebes have told ’s\nThey are sisters’ children, nephews to the King.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@35473/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 7,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@35473/line-2",
          "start": 8,
          "end": 46,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@35473/line-3",
          "start": 47,
          "end": 96,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@35473/line-4",
          "start": 97,
          "end": 145,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 6661731,
        "end": 6661916,
        "line": 249960,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap38/p@35473",
        "anchor": "sceneI_38.4"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "HERALD.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@35662",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "THESEUS.\nBy th’ helm of Mars, I saw them in the war,\nLike to a pair of lions, smeared with prey,\nMake lanes in troops aghast. I fixed my note\nConstantly on them, for they were a mark\nWorth a god’s view. What prisoner was ’t that told me\nWhen I enquired their names?",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@35662/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 8,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@35662/line-2",
          "start": 9,
          "end": 52,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@35662/line-3",
          "start": 53,
          "end": 96,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@35662/line-4",
          "start": 97,
          "end": 141,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@35662/line-5",
          "start": 142,
          "end": 182,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@35662/line-6",
          "start": 183,
          "end": 236,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@35662/line-7",
          "start": 237,
          "end": 265,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 6661920,
        "end": 6662240,
        "line": 249967,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap38/p@35662",
        "anchor": "sceneI_38.4"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "THESEUS.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@35986",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "HERALD.\nWi’ leave, they’re called Arcite and Palamon.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@35986/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 7,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@35986/line-2",
          "start": 8,
          "end": 53,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 6662244,
        "end": 6662327,
        "line": 249977,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap38/p@35986",
        "anchor": "sceneI_38.4"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "HERALD.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@36073",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "THESEUS.\n’Tis right; those, those. They are not dead?",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@36073/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 8,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@36073/line-2",
          "start": 9,
          "end": 53,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 6662331,
        "end": 6662414,
        "line": 249982,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap38/p@36073",
        "anchor": "sceneI_38.4"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "THESEUS.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@36160",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "HERALD.\nNor in a state of life. Had they been taken\nWhen their last hurts were given, ’twas possible\nThey might have been recovered; yet they breathe\nAnd have the name of men.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@36160/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 7,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@36160/line-2",
          "start": 8,
          "end": 51,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@36160/line-3",
          "start": 52,
          "end": 100,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@36160/line-4",
          "start": 101,
          "end": 149,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@36160/line-5",
          "start": 150,
          "end": 175,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 6662418,
        "end": 6662638,
        "line": 249987,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap38/p@36160",
        "anchor": "sceneI_38.4"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "HERALD.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@36384",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "THESEUS.\nThen like men use ’em.\nThe very lees of such, millions of rates,\nExceed the wine of others. All our surgeons\nConvent in their behoof; our richest balms,\nRather than niggard, waste. Their lives concern us\nMuch more than Thebes is worth. Rather than have ’em\nFreed of this plight, and in their morning state,\nSound and at liberty, I would ’em dead;\nBut forty-thousandfold we had rather have ’em\nPrisoners to us than death. Bear ’em speedily\nFrom our kind air, to them unkind, and minister\nWhat man to man may do, for our sake, more,\nSince I have known frights, fury, friends’ behests,\nLove’s provocations, zeal, a mistress’ task,\nDesire of liberty, a fever, madness,\nHath set a mark which nature could not reach to\nWithout some imposition, sickness in will\nO’er-wrestling strength in reason. For our love\nAnd great Apollo’s mercy, all our best\nTheir best skill tender. Lead into the city,\nWhere, having bound things scattered, we will post\nTo Athens ’fore our army.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@36384/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 8,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@36384/line-2",
          "start": 9,
          "end": 31,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@36384/line-3",
          "start": 32,
          "end": 73,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneI_38.4/p@36384/line-4",
          "start": 74,
          "end": 117,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
